Cell["\<\
Three events, one per edge. They are distinct as events but isomorphic as \
hypergraphs, which CanonicalHypergraph makes plain:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10dda6e1-27d5-534c-81d4-ca24d53d2e8f"],

Cell["\<\
Length @ DeleteDuplicates[CanonicalHypergraph[#[\"Hypergraph\"]] & /@ \
sub[star]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"932d55fd-0457-804b-9063-15310c56c490"],

Cell[BoxData["1"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"f0c98d44-da7c-4949-ae5c-e972714f372c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Distinct events with isomorphic results is the ordinary situation, not a \
special case, and it is why a multiway system has to decide whether its \
states are hypergraphs or isomorphism classes of them. The pieces for either \
reading are already here."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"b5289e83-ee1c-c94a-8fc9-38932c7924b7"],

Cell["An unordered rule", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"871a112d-02ea-5242-a41a-596f0799f68f"],

Cell["\<\
Nothing about rewriting is particular to directed edges. Here an unordered \
pair becomes an unordered triple:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0df1462c-d037-d14c-bc01-f7231ebd7243"],

Cell["\<\
grow = HypergraphRule[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"]},
                      {Edge[{1, 2, 3}, \"Unordered\"]}];
Length @ grow[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"]}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ff79a26f-a92d-5a42-926c-e426aba191a6"],

Cell[BoxData["2"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"6f1eca27-dc7b-3049-a7b1-c72bef3eedbc"],

Cell["\<\
Two events, from the two orderings the unordered pattern admits, and their \
results are the same hypergraph:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9e09ca1a-4b23-f64e-8018-cfcd6d81228d"],

Cell["\<\
DeleteDuplicates[#[\"Hypergraph\"] & /@ grow[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"25479acc-fe5c-b642-b19c-569df2101480"],

